ven. Saving Lives, Protecting People","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":125,"renderedHeight":81,"naturalWidth":233,"naturalHeight":150,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1262},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/5.0/img/logo/logo-notext.svg","alt":"Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. CDC twenty four seven. Saving Lives, Protecting People","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":233,"renderedHeight":150,"naturalWidth":233,"naturalHeight":150,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1262},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/cdc-hiv-trans-thumbnail.jpg","alt":"Group of transgender people.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":313,"renderedHeight":176,"naturalWidth":2560,"naturalHeight":1708,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":613630},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-05.png","alt":"Of the 36,801 new HIV diagnoses in the US and dependent areas in 2019, 2 percent (671) were among transgender people. The Ending the HIV Epidemic overall goal is to decrease the number of new HIV diagnoses to 9,588 by 2025 and 3,000 by 2030.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":232630},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2024/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-12.png","alt":"Most new HIV diagnoses among transgender people were among Black/African American people. Among transgender women, Black/African American people had the most new HIV diagnoses, followed by Hispanic/Latino, White, multiracial, Asian, American Indian/Alaska Native, and Native Hawaiian/other Pacific Islander people, respectively. Among transgender men, Black/African American people had the most new HIV diagnoses, followed by Hispanic/Latino, White, multiracial, and Asian people, respectively.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 494 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":341424},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-02.png","alt":"Among transgender people, most new HIV diagnoses were among people aged 25 to 34, followed by people aged 13 to 24, 35 to 44, 45 to 54, and 55 and older, respectively.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":274389},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-01.png","alt":"The highest number of new HIV diagnoses among transgender people were in the South, followed by transgender people in the West, Northeast, Midwest, and US Dependent Areas, respectively.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":222964},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-06.png","alt":"Trends in HIV diagnoses among transgender people varied by age. People 55 and older saw the largest increase in diagnoses, followed by people aged 25 to 34 and 35 to 44, respectively. People aged 45 to 54 saw the largest decrease in diagnoses, followed by people aged 13 to 24.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 277 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":173163},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2024/04/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-03.png","alt":"Getting test for HIV is the only way for people to learn their status. 96 percent of transgender women had ever tested for HIV. 82 percent of transgender women were tested for HIV in the past 12 months.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":257159},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-18.png","alt":"HIV prevention interventions can reduce risk behaviors. 61 percent of transgender women who do not have HIV participated in an individual or group level HIV prevention intervention.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":144136},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2024/04/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-04.png","alt":"PrEP is highly effective for preventing HIV from sex or injection drug use. 92 percent of transgender women without HIV were aware of PrEP. 32 percent of transgender women without HIV used PrEP.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":253037},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2024/04/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-07.png","alt":"Racial and ethnic disparities exist among transgender women with HIV. Among transgender women interviewed, 42 percent had HIV. 62 percent of Black/African American transgender women had HIV. 35 percent of Hispanic/Latina transgender women had HIV. 17 percent of White transgender women had HIV.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 294 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":441377},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-13.png","alt":"For every 100 transgender women with diagnosed HIV in 2019, 84 received some HIV care, 67 were retained in care, and 67 were virally suppressed. For every 100 transgender men with diagnosed HIV in 2019, 85 received some HIV care, 65 were retained in care, and 68 were virally suppressed. For comparison, for every 100 people overall with diagnosed HIV, 76 received some HIV care, 58 were retained in care, and 66 were virally suppressed.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 437 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":448613},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-17.png","alt":"Staying in HIV care is important to achieving and maintaining viral suppression. 20 percent of all people with HIV, compared to 31 percent of transgender people with HIV, missed at least 1 medical appointment in the past 12 months.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":270452},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-16.png","alt":"Taking HIV medicine consistently and as prescribed is the bast way to achieve and maintain viral suppression. 62 percent of all people with HIV, compared to 35 percent of transgender people with HIV, reported taking all of their doses of HIV medicine over the last 30 days.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2814,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 273 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":324118},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-09.png","alt":"HIV ancillary care services are essential for supporting people in staying in HIV care and maintaining viral suppression. The top service transgender people with HIV reported needing in 2020 was dental care, with 17 percent saying they needed but did not receive it. 41 percent of all people with HIV needed, but did not receive, at least 1 HIV ancillary service in the past 12 months.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 385 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":233127},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-15.png","alt":"People who experience homelessness may find it difficult to get HIV care and treatment. 8 percent of all people with HIV, compared to 29 percent of transgender people with HIV, reported homelessness in the past 12 months.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":265395},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2024/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-14.png","alt":"Some transgender people with diagnosed HIV may have difficulty getting treatment. 19 percent of all people with HIV, compared to 26 percent of transgender people with HIV, experienced symptoms of depression or anxiety in the past 12 months.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":271338},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/hiv/media/images/2025/03/Transgender-web-content-2023_DFE-08_1.png","alt":"Transgender people with HIV experienced HIV stigma. On a scale of 1 to 100, with 100 representing high HIV stigma and 0 representing no HIV stigma, all people with HIV had a score of 28, while transgender people with HIV had a score of 34. The goal is 0 for all populations.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":658,"renderedHeight":370,"naturalWidth":5001,"naturalHeight":2813,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 274 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":303931},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/5.0/img/logo/cdc-logo-tag-right.svg","alt":"Centers for Disease Control and Prevention","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":282,"renderedHeight":66,"naturalWidth":827,"naturalHeight":193,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":4780}]},"thirdParty":{"engine":"third-party","pageUrl":"http://www.cdc.gov/hiv/data-research/facts-stats/transgender-people.html","thirdPartyOrigins":2,"scriptOrigins":1,"totalThirdPartyRequests":2,"totalThirdPartyBytes":158090,"totalThirdPartyScripts":1,"firstPartyRequests":130,"firstPartyBytes":29724107,"origins":[{"origin":"googletagmanager.com","requests":1,"bytes":158090,"scripts":1,"byType":{"script":1},"totalDurationMs":2},{"origin":"google-analytics.com","requests":1,"bytes":0,"scripts":0,"byType":{"fetch":1},"totalDurationMs":13}]}}